{
  "note": "One-piece, 20 mm diameter knob with a blind, captive M3 hex-nut pocket. The nut is pressed in from the bed-side opening through a slightly undersized retaining throat; six relief slits let the throat flex. The nut sits below a solid roof, and a 3.5 mm axial bore passes through the nut position and out the opposite face. Use with an M3 threaded bolt or stud; no bolt length is assumed. The slits and nut pocket print open-side-down without supports; the short pocket roof bridge is only about 5.7 mm. Press-fit retention depends on printer/material variation, so check that the nut seats and stays captured before putting it into service.",
  "params": {
